{"id": "striviaqa0060", "pool": "striviaqa", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 328215125, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "760971df1e172c7bf1d6bc3b4ee980bf878d27e27419c4254baabbe495a6c145", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Which singer released the albums Honky Chateau in 1972 and Sleeping with the Past in 1989?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/striviaqa0060.wav", "input_sha256": "f9b65779af9f734131db6819f611de3c76214b9fd7dd68e1b948b05a53a2bccf", "input_samples": 155074, "input_s": 9.692, "n_real_chunks": 10, "score": 0.7869, "act": 1.0, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "That was the singer Rod St ewart. He released the album Honky Chateau in 1 9 7 2, which became one of his biggest success es and helped solidify his status as a top artist during that era. The album featured hit s like \"Maggie May\" and \"You Wear It Well,\" which were major chart toppers at the time. Later on, in 1 98 9, he released Sleeping with the Past, marking a shift in his sound toward more mature and introspective material. So, Rod Stewart is the artist behind both those albums.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 9, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 36, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/striviaqa/audio/striviaqa0060_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "eec6e98c20377289d8d260e780d619ccc5cf8d56da4cd3b6527feb763849e225", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 35.4}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.072, 1.126, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.072, 2.131, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.085